1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,940
Meet the price tag, then meet the bill. A

2
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:04,980
pair of shoes is marked at four hundred and

3
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:08,158
fifty rupees. At the counter, a sales tax of

4
00:00:08,158 --> 00:00:12,700
six percent is added. Three quantities are involved: the

5
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,400
base price, the price before any tax; the tax

6
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:18,650
amount, the percentage that is added; and the final

7
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:21,062
bill, the base price plus the tax. So the

8
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,971
tag and the bill show two different numbers.

9
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:26,649
A tax is just a percentage increase. The original

10
00:00:26,649 --> 00:00:29,397
price is taken as one hundred percent. Adding a

11
00:00:29,397 --> 00:00:31,493
tax of r percent gives one hundred plus r

12
00:00:31,493 --> 00:00:35,093
percent. With six percent, the total becomes one hundred

13
00:00:35,093 --> 00:00:38,113
and six percent. So the final bill is one

14
00:00:38,113 --> 00:00:40,337
hundred plus r, divided by one hundred, times the

15
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:43,383
base price. This is exactly the percentage increase we

16
00:00:43,383 --> 00:00:44,824
met in the earlier lesson.

17
00:00:45,447 --> 00:00:47,078
Now the same shoes, with the numbers filled in.

18
00:00:47,078 --> 00:00:49,397
The base price is four hundred and fifty rupees.

19
00:00:49,397 --> 00:00:51,432
Sales tax is six percent, so the tax is

20
00:00:51,432 --> 00:00:54,454
six over one hundred times four hundred and fifty,

21
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:56,932
which is twenty seven rupees. Add it to the

22
00:00:56,932 --> 00:01:00,847
base price: four hundred and fifty plus twenty seven

23
00:01:00,847 --> 00:01:02,667
is four hundred and seventy seven rupees. Here is

24
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:05,949
the shortcut: one hundred and six percent of four

25
00:01:05,949 --> 00:01:08,667
hundred and fifty. That is one point zero six

26
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:11,787
times four hundred and fifty, which is again four

27
00:01:11,787 --> 00:01:13,498
hundred and seventy seven rupees.

28
00:01:14,213 --> 00:01:16,937
A tax can also be written on the bill.

29
00:01:16,937 --> 00:01:20,273
Here is a medical bill: the amount before value

30
00:01:20,273 --> 00:01:23,813
added tax is three hundred and fifty four rupees

31
00:01:23,813 --> 00:01:25,701
and forty five paise. The value added tax is

32
00:01:25,701 --> 00:01:29,533
five percent, which is seventeen rupees and seventy two

33
00:01:29,533 --> 00:01:31,353
paise. The total is three hundred and seventy two

34
00:01:31,353 --> 00:01:33,905
rupees and eighteen paise, so the base plus the

35
00:01:33,905 --> 00:01:37,462
tax gives the bill. Value added tax works exactly

36
00:01:37,462 --> 00:01:40,493
like the sales tax we just used: both are

37
00:01:40,493 --> 00:01:44,247
the same percentage idea. And remember, these older rates

38
00:01:44,247 --> 00:01:47,569
are textbook and historical examples, not advice about the

39
00:01:47,569 --> 00:01:49,364
taxes of today.

40
00:01:50,080 --> 00:01:52,467
Goods and services tax uses the same structure. GST

41
00:01:52,467 --> 00:01:56,183
is an indirect tax on goods and services, and

42
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:58,407
it is charged on the base price. Take a

43
00:01:58,407 --> 00:02:01,388
base price of one thousand rupees, with GST at

44
00:02:01,388 --> 00:02:05,464
five percent. Five percent of one thousand is fifty

45
00:02:05,464 --> 00:02:09,020
rupees, so the tax amount is fifty rupees. Add

46
00:02:09,020 --> 00:02:12,680
it to the base: one thousand plus fifty is

47
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:17,280
one thousand and fifty rupees. The shortcut is unchanged:

48
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:19,500
one hundred and five percent of one thousand is

49
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:21,751
also one thousand and fifty.

50
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:25,334
Now the other direction. A bill of two thousand

51
00:02:25,334 --> 00:02:28,091
three hundred and sixty rupees already includes GST at

52
00:02:28,091 --> 00:02:31,776
eighteen percent. So this bill is not one hundred

53
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:34,440
percent: it is one hundred and eighteen percent of

54
00:02:34,440 --> 00:02:38,089
the base price. To recover the base price we

55
00:02:38,089 --> 00:02:42,080
divide: two thousand three hundred and sixty times one

56
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:46,240
hundred, over one hundred and eighteen. That gives a

57
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:50,260
base price of two thousand rupees, and the tax

58
00:02:50,260 --> 00:02:53,527
is the rest, three hundred and sixty rupees. Never

59
00:02:53,527 --> 00:02:56,338
take eighteen percent of two thousand three hundred and

60
00:02:56,338 --> 00:02:58,994
sixty and subtract it: the rate was charged on

61
00:02:58,994 --> 00:03:00,791
the base, not on the bill.

62
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:04,393
Here is a worked example from the textbook. The

63
00:03:04,393 --> 00:03:06,253
total GST on that purchase is three hundred and

64
00:03:06,253 --> 00:03:08,911
sixty rupees. In this worked example the tax is

65
00:03:08,911 --> 00:03:13,265
divided into two equal parts. One half is central

66
00:03:13,265 --> 00:03:16,575
GST, one hundred and eighty rupees. The other half

67
00:03:16,575 --> 00:03:19,091
is state GST, another one hundred and eighty rupees.

68
00:03:19,091 --> 00:03:22,253
So one block of three hundred and sixty splits

69
00:03:22,253 --> 00:03:24,573
into one hundred and eighty and one hundred and

70
00:03:24,573 --> 00:03:27,933
eighty. That equal split belongs to this worked example,

71
00:03:27,933 --> 00:03:30,104
not to every bill.

72
00:03:30,727 --> 00:03:33,781
Now a two lane decision board. If the base

73
00:03:33,781 --> 00:03:36,347
price is given, go forward: find the tax, then

74
00:03:36,347 --> 00:03:38,627
add it, or use the bill equals the base

75
00:03:38,627 --> 00:03:41,827
times one hundred plus r, over one hundred. If

76
00:03:41,827 --> 00:03:47,227
the tax-inclusive bill is given, go backward: recover the

77
00:03:47,227 --> 00:03:50,167
base with base equals bill times one hundred, over

78
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:52,967
one hundred plus r. Which lane you use depends

79
00:03:52,967 --> 00:03:55,713
only on what you were given. And keep tax

80
00:03:55,713 --> 00:03:59,191
separate from discount: a discount is taken away from

81
00:03:59,191 --> 00:04:02,827
the price, while a tax is added to the

82
00:04:02,827 --> 00:04:04,758
base. Tax adds, discount removes.

83
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,520
Here is the classic error. Take a base price

84
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:11,600
of one thousand rupees, with GST at eighteen percent.

85
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:15,564
The tax is eighteen percent of one thousand, which

86
00:04:15,564 --> 00:04:18,587
is one hundred and eighty rupees, so the bill

87
00:04:18,587 --> 00:04:21,318
is one thousand one hundred and eighty. The mistake

88
00:04:21,318 --> 00:04:24,226
is to apply the rate to the bill: eighteen

89
00:04:24,226 --> 00:04:26,600
percent of one thousand one hundred and eighty is

90
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:29,890
not the tax for this purchase. The same mistake

91
00:04:29,890 --> 00:04:32,170
is to subtract the rate straight off a tax-inclusive

92
00:04:32,170 --> 00:04:35,400
bill. The rate is always applied to the base,

93
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,337
and a tax-inclusive bill is worked backward with one

94
00:04:38,337 --> 00:04:40,311
hundred over one hundred plus r.

95
00:04:40,967 --> 00:04:44,740
Your turn. Four quick checks. A: an item costs

96
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:46,792
eight hundred rupees, and the tax is five percent.

97
00:04:46,792 --> 00:04:49,287
What is the tax, and what is the bill?

98
00:04:49,287 --> 00:04:52,567
B: a bill of one thousand one hundred and

99
00:04:52,567 --> 00:04:56,027
eighty rupees includes GST at eighteen percent. What is

100
00:04:56,027 --> 00:04:58,107
the base price, and what is the tax? C:

101
00:04:58,107 --> 00:05:01,774
a total GST of one hundred and eighty rupees

102
00:05:01,774 --> 00:05:04,785
is split equally into central GST and state GST.

103
00:05:04,785 --> 00:05:07,039
How much is each part? D: here is the

104
00:05:07,039 --> 00:05:11,857
error to spot. Eighteen percent of one thousand rupees

105
00:05:11,857 --> 00:05:14,747
is one hundred and eighty rupees, so is eighteen

106
00:05:14,747 --> 00:05:17,009
percent of one thousand one hundred and eighty the

107
00:05:17,009 --> 00:05:19,927
right tax for the same purchase? Pause the video,

108
00:05:19,927 --> 00:05:24,278
work all four out, and then we will check every answer.

109
00:05:35,367 --> 00:05:38,647
Let us check every answer. A: five percent of

110
00:05:38,647 --> 00:05:41,007
eight hundred is forty rupees, so the tax is

111
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:44,047
forty rupees and the bill is eight hundred and

112
00:05:44,047 --> 00:05:47,687
forty rupees. B: the bill is one hundred and

113
00:05:47,687 --> 00:05:49,799
eighteen percent, so the base is one thousand one

114
00:05:49,799 --> 00:05:54,147
hundred and eighty times one hundred over one hundred

115
00:05:54,147 --> 00:05:56,437
and eighteen, which is one thousand rupees, and the

116
00:05:56,437 --> 00:06:00,567
tax is one hundred and eighty rupees. C: one

117
00:06:00,567 --> 00:06:03,311
hundred and eighty split equally is ninety and ninety,

118
00:06:03,311 --> 00:06:05,867
so central GST is ninety rupees and state GST

119
00:06:05,867 --> 00:06:09,617
is ninety rupees. D: no. Eighteen percent of one

120
00:06:09,617 --> 00:06:11,697
thousand one hundred and eighty is not the tax

121
00:06:11,697 --> 00:06:13,971
for this purchase. The rate belongs on the base

122
00:06:13,971 --> 00:06:15,278
of one thousand rupees.

123
00:06:15,773 --> 00:06:18,213
One last look. Start at one hundred percent, the

124
00:06:18,213 --> 00:06:21,423
base price. Add the tax to reach one hundred

125
00:06:21,423 --> 00:06:24,077
plus r percent. Work backward with one hundred divided

126
00:06:24,077 --> 00:06:27,433
by one hundred plus r when the tax-inclusive total

127
00:06:27,433 --> 00:06:30,626
is given. And keep the tax separate from a

128
00:06:30,626 --> 00:06:33,073
discount: a tax adds to the base, a discount

129
00:06:33,073 --> 00:06:36,516
takes off the price. So start at one hundred

130
00:06:36,516 --> 00:06:40,270
percent, add the tax, and work backward with one

131
00:06:40,270 --> 00:06:43,310
hundred divided by one hundred plus r. Thank you

132
00:06:43,310 --> 00:06:45,444
for watching, and see you in the next lesson.
